  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 in account ACC-1005. The amount is **EUR 240.00**, paid by card to **TechMart Online** on 2026-07-20. The status is settled.\n\nYour account also shows **TX-0402**, a card payment of EUR 240.00 to the same merchant on 2026-07-14. If you think you were charged twice, that is the most relevant match.\n\nBased only on the transaction details, these reason codes could apply, depending on what happened:\n\n- **duplicate_charge**: You were charged more than once for the same purchase. TX-0401 and TX-0402 match on amount and merchant, so this may fit if they were for the same order.\n- **unauthorized_debit**: You did not authorise this payment.\n- **fraud_card_not_present**: The payment was made online or by card details without your involvement, such as through a compromised card number.\n- **goods_not_received**: You paid for goods that were never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered**: You paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nTell me which situation matches what happened, and I will check whether a dispute can be opened under that code. I will not open anything until you confirm.",
